    description: "All 103 event_publishes edges are synthesized by the message-queue linker from MQ pattern example strings (producer.send('topic'), consumer.subscribe(['topic'])) embedded as STRING LITERALS in three regression-test files; 26 of them link a 'publisher' in one test file to a 'subscriber' in a different, unrelated test file by topic match. src files: test_linker_docstring_fp_regression.py(15), test_linkers_text_filters.py(20), test_message_queue_linker.py(68). Node records: kind=function, origin=['message-queue-linker'], name='kafka:publish:topic'/'kafka:subscribe:topic', supply_chain.is_test_file=True. Sample edge: test_linker_docstring_fp_regression.py:27-27:mq_publisher -> test_linkers_text_filters.py:52-52:mq_subscriber (evidence_type=topic_match, conf=0.9). Consequence: a consumer reading the behavior map sees phantom event-flow edges between unrelated modules; an LLM auditing pub/sub coupling concludes these test files communicate via Kafka. False positives in a Tier-2 edge-recovery linker."  # a126
